IMPORT prelude

-- Estate Agents Act 2010 (Singapore) -- what counts as estate agency work and who is outside the Act (ss 3, 4), the licensing
-- and registration offences and the bar on recovering commission (ss 28, 29, 44), who may be licensed or registered (ss 3(2),
-- 30, 32, 32A), the disciplinary penalty caps (ss 49(6), 52(12), (13)) and whether an appeal stays a revocation (s 59(3), (4)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation,
-- "version in force from 1/7/2025", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EAA2010.txt. The latest amendment annotated
-- in the text is Act 15 of 2025 with effect from 1 July 2025.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone in Singapore who sells, buys or rents a home through an agent
-- meets this Act, and anyone who helps a friend find a buyer for a fee may be within it. SCOPED to the provisions a home
-- owner, buyer, tenant or would-be salesperson meets. Not encoded: the Council for Estate Agencies (Part 2), applications,
-- duration and the register (ss 33-37), key executive officers and agent-salesperson agreements (ss 38, 39, 41), codes of
-- practice and reporting (ss 42-43A), the anti-money-laundering duties of Part 4A beyond their penalty caps, inspectors'
-- powers (ss 45-47), Disciplinary Committee procedure (ss 51, 53-56), the Appeals Board's constitution and procedure, the
-- general offences of s 64 and the regulations. Ministerial exemptions and exclusions (s 5) and regulations excluding work
-- from s 44 (s 44(4)) are not modelled: the encoding assumes none applies.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Estate Agents Act 2010 -- estate agents and salespersons`

§§ `3(1), (3) -- estate agency work`

-- s 3(1): "estate agency work" means "any work done in the course of business for a client or any work done for or in
-- expectation of any fee (whether or not in the course of business) for a client", being work (a) "in relation to the
-- introduction to the client of a third person who wishes to acquire or dispose of a property, or to the negotiation for the
-- acquisition or disposition of a property by the client"; or (b) after that introduction or negotiation, in relation to the
-- acquisition or disposition. "purchaser" includes "a prospective tenant"; "vendor" includes "a prospective landlord".
-- s 3(3)(a): not "work which relates solely to a survey, to a valuation or to a disposition by way of auction or tender".
--
-- A one-off introduction for a fee is estate agency work even though it is not a business.
GIVEN `in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN, `for or in expectation of a fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `introducing or negotiating a property deal for a client` IS A BOOLEAN, `solely a survey, valuation, auction or tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is estate agency work` IF
        (`in the course of business` OR `for or in expectation of a fee`)
    AND `introducing or negotiating a property deal for a client`
    AND (NOT `solely a survey, valuation, auction or tender`)

§§ `4(1) -- excluded activities and persons`

-- s 4(1): "This Act does not apply to anything done" (a) by an executor, administrator, trustee, liquidator, receiver or trustee
-- in bankruptcy performing those functions; (b) by a solicitor in practice introducing third persons "if the solicitor ... do[es]
-- not perform any other work that falls within the definition of 'estate agency work'"; (c) by an appraiser valuing; (d) "in
-- connection with a mortgage or other charge on property"; (e) publishing advertisements or disseminating information by a person
-- "who does no other work" within the definition; (f) by a vendor or purchaser in connection with the disposition or acquisition
-- of the property; (g) by an employee on the employer's instructions where (f) would cover the employer; (h) in relation to the
-- person's own present, prospective or former employee "by reason of the employment"; (i) by the Government or a public body
-- acting for the Government or exercising a public function.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `an owner selling their own flat`
    `a tenant looking for a flat for themselves`
    `an executor selling the deceased's house`
    `a solicitor who only introduces a buyer`
    `a solicitor who also negotiates the price`
    `a listings portal that only publishes advertisements`
    `a bank arranging a mortgage`
    `an employer finding housing for its employee`
    `a statutory board acting for the Government`
    `a friend introducing a buyer for a fee`
    `a property agency firm`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act does not apply to what the actor does` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `a solicitor who also negotiates the price` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a friend introducing a buyer for a fee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a property agency firm` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `28, 29 -- licensing and registration offences`

-- s 28(1): a person must not carry on or advertise the business of estate agency work, "act as an estate agent", or hold himself
-- or herself out as ready to undertake estate agency work "whether or not for payment", "unless he or she is a licensed estate
-- agent". (2) a fine up to $75,000 or 3 years or both, and for a continuing offence "a further fine not exceeding $7,500 for every
-- day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `acts as or holds out as an estate agent` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a licensed estate agent` IS A BOOLEAN, `is outside the Act under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unlicensed estate agency is an offence` IF
        `acts as or holds out as an estate agent`
    AND (NOT `is a licensed estate agent`)
    AND (NOT `is outside the Act under section 4`)

GIVEN `days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed estate agency` MEANS
    75000 PLUS 7500 TIMES `days the offence continues after conviction`

-- s 29(1): (a) a person must not be or act as a salesperson for a licensed estate agent, or hold out as one, "unless he or she is
-- a registered salesperson"; (b) must not accept employment as, or act as, a salesperson for a person "who is required by this
-- Act to hold, but is not the holder of, an estate agent's licence". (3) a fine up to $25,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `acts as a salesperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a registered salesperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agency is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `acting as a salesperson is an offence` IF
        `acts as a salesperson`
    AND ((NOT `is a registered salesperson`) OR (NOT `the agency is licensed`))

§§ `28(3), 29(4), 44 -- recovering commission and outgoings`

-- s 28(3), 29(4): "No fee, commission or reward in relation to anything done by a person in respect of an offence under this
-- section is recoverable in any action, suit or matter by any person."
-- s 44(1): a cause of action for "agreed sums, damages or any other relief" lies at the suit of the estate agent "if, and only
-- if" (a) an estate agency agreement in the prescribed form with the prescribed particulars has been entered into and, if
-- written, properly executed; and (b) "the estate agent was a licensed estate agent at the time when the estate agency agreement
-- was so entered into and executed". (2) outgoings are recoverable only if, in addition, "(b) the estate agency agreement
-- expressly provides for such recovery or reimbursement".
--
-- Being licensed later does not help: the licence must exist when the agreement is executed.
GIVEN `a prescribed-form agreement was entered into and executed` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensed when the agreement was executed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the work was done in an offence under section 28 or 29` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agent can sue for the commission` IF
        `a prescribed-form agreement was entered into and executed`
    AND `licensed when the agreement was executed`
    AND (NOT `the work was done in an offence under section 28 or 29`)

GIVEN `a prescribed-form agreement was entered into and executed` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensed when the agreement was executed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agreement expressly provides for reimbursement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agent can recover outgoings` IF
        `a prescribed-form agreement was entered into and executed`
    AND `licensed when the agreement was executed`
    AND `the agreement expressly provides for reimbursement`

§§ `3(2), 30, 32 -- who may be licensed or registered`

-- s 3(2): a person is not fit and proper if the Council is of that view, "and unless the Council otherwise determines" an
-- individual is not fit and proper if he or she (i) "has been convicted of an offence involving dishonesty or fraud"; (ii) has a
-- civil judgment involving "a finding of fraud, dishonesty or breach of fiduciary duties"; (iia) has been convicted of an offence
-- involving money laundering, proliferation financing or terrorism financing "(whether in Singapore or elsewhere)"; (iii) "has
-- been convicted of any offence under this Act"; or (iv) "is an undischarged bankrupt or has made a composition or arrangement
-- with his or her creditors".
DECLARE Individual HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `has the prescribed qualifications or approved experience` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a salesperson of another licensed estate agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is or will be employed by a licensed estate agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a licence as another estate agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds or works for a moneylender's licence holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the other prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of dishonesty or fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a civil judgment for fraud or breach of fiduciary duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of money laundering or terrorism financing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt or in a composition with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Council otherwise determines` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Council considers the individual unfit` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual has a listed disqualification` IF
        `the individual`'s `convicted of dishonesty or fraud`
    OR  `the individual`'s `has a civil judgment for fraud or breach of fiduciary duty`
    OR  `the individual`'s `convicted of money laundering or terrorism financing`
    OR  `the individual`'s `convicted under this Act`
    OR  `the individual`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt or in a composition with creditors`

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is fit and proper` IF
        (NOT `the individual`'s `the Council considers the individual unfit`)
    AND ((NOT `the individual has a listed disqualification` `the individual`) OR `the individual`'s `the Council otherwise determines`)

-- s 30: an individual is not eligible to hold an estate agent's licence unless (a) "the individual has attained 21 years of age"
-- (or a prescribed age); (b) has prescribed qualifications, courses, examinations and experience or Council-approved training or
-- experience; (c) "is not a salesperson of any other licensed estate agent"; (d) "does not hold and is not an employee, a
-- director or a partner of a person who holds a moneylender's licence"; (e) meets other prescribed requirements; and (f) is fit
-- and proper. The prescribed age is not read; 21 is used.
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is eligible for an estate agent's licence` IF
        `the individual`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the individual`'s `has the prescribed qualifications or approved experience`
    AND (NOT `the individual`'s `is a salesperson of another licensed estate agent`)
    AND (NOT `the individual`'s `holds or works for a moneylender's licence holder`)
    AND `the individual`'s `meets the other prescribed requirements`
    AND `the individual is fit and proper` `the individual`

-- s 32(1): "Only a natural person may be registered as a salesperson." (2) not eligible unless (a) 21 years of age (or prescribed);
-- (b) (i) "is or will be employed by a licensed estate agent as a salesperson and he or she does not hold a licence as any other
-- estate agent"; (ii) prescribed educational qualifications or experience; (iii) no moneylender link; (iv) other prescribed
-- requirements "including continuing education"; and (c) fit and proper.
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is eligible to be a registered salesperson` IF
        `the individual`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the individual`'s `is or will be employed by a licensed estate agent`
    AND (NOT `the individual`'s `holds a licence as another estate agent`)
    AND `the individual`'s `has the prescribed qualifications or approved experience`
    AND (NOT `the individual`'s `holds or works for a moneylender's licence holder`)
    AND `the individual`'s `meets the other prescribed requirements`
    AND `the individual is fit and proper` `the individual`

-- s 32A(2): "In addition to section 32", the Council (a) "may refuse to register or renew the registration" of a salesperson who
-- has an unpaid financial penalty under s 49(6)(a)(iii) or (b)(i), 52(3) or 66(3)(a); and (b) "may refuse to renew" if the
-- individual "has not satisfied the CPE requirements". A discretion, not a bar.
GIVEN `has an unpaid financial penalty` IS A BOOLEAN, `has satisfied the CPE requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may refuse to renew the registration` IF
    `has an unpaid financial penalty` OR (NOT `has satisfied the CPE requirements`)

§§ `49(6), 52(12), (13) -- disciplinary financial penalties`

-- s 49(6): the Council itself may impose a financial penalty "not exceeding $5,000 for each contravention" of the anti-money-
-- laundering requirements (Part 4A and the related regulations and codes), and "not exceeding $5,000" for any other sufficient
-- cause, and may censure.
-- s 52(12): a Disciplinary Committee's maximum for sufficient cause other than such a contravention is "(a) in the case of a
-- licensed estate agent -- $200,000; and (b) in the case of a registered salesperson -- $100,000". (13): for those anti-money-
-- laundering contraventions the same figures apply "for each contravention".
DECLARE Licensee IS ONE OF
    `a licensed estate agent`
    `a registered salesperson`

GIVEN `the licensee` IS A Licensee
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Committee's base cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the licensee`
    WHEN `a licensed estate agent` THEN 200000
    OTHERWISE 100000

GIVEN `the licensee` IS A Licensee, `an anti-money-laundering contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of contraventions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Disciplinary Committee's maximum penalty` MEANS
    IF `an anti-money-laundering contravention`
    THEN `the Committee's base cap` `the licensee` TIMES `number of contraventions`
    ELSE `the Committee's base cap` `the licensee`

GIVEN `an anti-money-laundering contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of contraventions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Council's maximum penalty` MEANS
    IF `an anti-money-laundering contravention`
    THEN 5000 TIMES `number of contraventions`
    ELSE 5000

§§ `59(3), (4) -- does an appeal stop the order?`

-- s 59(3): "the lodging of an appeal ... does not suspend the effect of the decision to which the appeal relates". (4) but where
-- the order revokes or suspends a licence or registration and the licensee or salesperson "gives due notice of appeal", the order
-- "is stayed pending the determination of the appeal unless the Appeals Board, on the application of the Council, orders
-- otherwise".
GIVEN `the order revokes or suspends a licence or registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `due notice of appeal was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Appeals Board orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is stayed pending appeal` IF
        `the order revokes or suspends a licence or registration`
    AND `due notice of appeal was given`
    AND (NOT `the Appeals Board orders otherwise`)
